# Agreeing on a derivable skeleton proves the structural half only if the two
# also agree on what is not derivable. Each case breaks one thing: an
# occurrence the artifact does not have, a premise whose notion does not chain,
# a value the sealed protocol supplies and a caller may not, a target the root
# does not reach.
#
# REQUIRES: uv
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: zkc-seal %S/../Encoding/sumcheck-fs.mlir %zkc-seal-full -o %t/sealed.artifacts > /dev/null
# RUN: %python %S/../SemanticClosure/lib/artifact_handoff.py stage %t/sealed.artifacts %t/sealed.mlirbc
# RUN: %uv python %S/Inputs/request_mutations.py \
# RUN:   %S/Inputs/sumcheck-fs-request.json %t/sealed.mlirbc \
# RUN:   %zkc-registry-dir/soundness-signature.json \
# RUN:   %zkc-registry-dir/protocol-vocabulary.json \
# RUN:   %zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json zkc-derive \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: unexpected exceptions escape the refusal boundary
# The control is asserted, not merely run: a non-zero exit is evidence of
# refusal only while the tool is known to derive something.
# CHECK: control: the unmutated request derives
# CHECK: 19/19 refused by both
